================================================================================
Managed native SQLite runtime
================================================================================

SQLite3 Multiple Ciphers 2.5.1
  Copyright (c) 2019-2026 Ulrich Telle
  https://utelle.github.io/SQLite3MultipleCiphers/

  Licensed under the MIT License in LICENSE-SQLITE3MULTIPLECIPHERS.

  FinGrind vendors the official SQLite3 Multiple Ciphers 2.5.1 amalgamation based on SQLite 3.53.4. The managed library compiles the upstream built-in AES, ChaCha20, SQLCipher, RC4, Ascon, and AEGIS implementations; FinGrind's supported protected-book contract selects the upstream default sqleet / ChaCha20 format. Embedded SHA-2, AEGIS, Argon2, PBKDF2, and public-domain implementation notices are in LICENSE-SQLITE3MULTIPLECIPHERS-THIRD-PARTY. Apache 2.0 and CC0 1.0 texts referenced by those notices accompany the distribution.

SQLite 3.53.4
  https://www.sqlite.org/

  SQLite's authors dedicate the SQLite code to the public domain. The official copyright statement and warranty-of-title information are at https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html. FinGrind conveys SQLite through the SQLite3 Multiple Ciphers amalgamation.

  The application JAR does not contain the native library. Self-contained bundles and the container convey it as a sibling managed native artifact; source-checkout execution uses the repository-built managed artifact.

