Linked Java runtime in self-contained bundles and the container
================================================================================

Azul Zulu 26.32 / OpenJDK 26.0.2.1+1
  https://docs.azul.com/core/tpls/august-2026/zulu26_jdk_tpl.html

  Public bundles and the container contain a jlink-created runtime derived from Azul Zulu/OpenJDK, not merely MIT-licensed FinGrind code. OpenJDK portions are governed by GNU GPL version 2 with the Classpath Exception; assembly exceptions and module-specific third-party terms also apply.

  Each artifact preserves the complete selected-module legal tree under runtime/legal/<module>/ with runtime/legal/INDEX.sha256, records the linked module closure in runtime/release, and copies the source JDK's exact vendor/build metadata to runtime/provenance/source-jdk-release. The container additionally records the verified input JDK binary archive name and digest. SOURCE_OFFER.md supplies the corresponding-source route that accompanies the object code. The indexed runtime/legal tree, rather than this summary, is the authority for the modules actually present in an artifact.

================================================================================
Container-only operating-system layer
================================================================================

The production image's pinned Alpine Linux 3.24 base currently resolves Alpine 3.24.1 on both published architectures. Alpine packages remain governed by their package-specific GPL, MPL, Apache, MIT, BSD, Zlib, and other terms. They are not covered by FinGrind's MIT license.

The final image records every installed package's exact name, version, source-package origin, Alpine packaging commit, upstream URL, and declared SPDX-style license expression at:
  /opt/fingrind/doc/ALPINE-PACKAGES.tsv

The generated inventory must byte-match the reviewed `gradle/alpine-container-packages.lock.tsv` before the image can build. LICENSE-ALPINE-CONTAINER-COMPONENTS reproduces available musl, zlib, OpenSSL, and musl-utils notices, discloses the Alpine data-package notice limitation, and routes each exact source package. LICENSE-GPL-2.0 and LICENSE-MPL-2.0 provide the reciprocal license texts, while SOURCE_OFFER.md covers corresponding source. The original APK database remains at /lib/apk/db/installed. BuildKit SBOM and provenance attestations supplement this human-readable payload but do not replace licenses, notices, or source availability.

